## ldes:EventStream ## {#EventStream}

The class `ldes:EventStream` is a subclass of `dcat:Distribution`: an ordered log of immutable members, published as one specific view of a `dcat:Dataset`, which makes the log append-only. Each member is published as an RDF Message. The IRI of the LDES always dereferences to its root `ldes:Page`. In a DCAT-AP catalog, `dcat:accessURL` of the distribution is used for the entry point, but not within the pages of the LDES. It is loosely aligned with `tree:Collection`, but unlike that class it is not the dataset itself.

Issue: Making the LDES a distribution instead of the dataset is a change compared to LDES 1.0 that still needs to be discussed.

## ldes:shape ## {#shape}

Links the event stream to a `sh:NodeShape` that every member is intended to conform to. Aligned with `tree:shape`.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** `sh:NodeShape`

## ldes:timestampPath ## {#timestampPath}

The path to the `xsd:dateTime` literal in each member that defines the order of the event stream.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** a [SHACL property path](https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/#property-paths)

## ldes:sequencePath ## {#sequencePath}

The path to an `xsd`-typed literal in each member that defines the order of the event stream in addition to the `ldes:timestampPath`.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** a [SHACL property path](https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/#property-paths)


## ldes:versionOfPath ## {#versionOfPath}

The path to the IRI in each member that defines the entity of which this member is a version.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** a [SHACL property path](https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/#property-paths)


## ldes:versionTimestampPath ## {#versionTimestampPath}

For out-of-order event streams, this defines the path to the `xsd:dateTime` literal in each member that defines the order of versioned members.

Only relevant when the `ldes:versionOfPath` has been set.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** a [SHACL property path](https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/#property-paths)

## ldes:versionSequencePath ## {#versionSequencePath}

For out-of-order event streams, this defines the path to an `xsd`-typed literal in each member that defines the order of the event stream in addition to the `ldes:versionTimestampPath`.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** a [SHACL property path](https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/#property-paths)

## ldes:pollingInterval ## {#pollingInterval}

The number of seconds the client should keep between synchronization run calls.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`
**Range:** `xsd:integer`

## ldes:immutable ## {#immutable}

If the node is not going to contain new relations leading to new members, or new members itself, it can be set to immutable.

**Domain:** `ldes:Page`
**Range:** `xsd:boolean`

## ldes:Page ## {#Page}

A page of a view, published as an RDF Message log when it contains members. It does not have to be stated explicitly: it follows from the domain of `ldes:relation`. A subclass of `tree:Node`.

## Relations between pages ## {#relations}

### ldes:Relation ### {#Relation}

A link from a page to another page, annotated with an interval of the ordering key of the members that can be found by following it. Can have additional types and properties, such as the relation types of TREE. A subclass of `tree:Relation`.

### ldes:relation ### {#relation}

Links a page to a relation. A subproperty of `tree:relation`.

**Domain:** `ldes:Page`

**Range:** `ldes:Relation`

### ldes:page ### {#pageProperty}

The page to dereference when following the relation. A subproperty of `tree:node`.

**Domain:** `ldes:Relation`

**Range:** `ldes:Page`

### ldes:timeFrom ### {#timeFrom}

Inclusive lower bound of the `ldes:timestampPath` value of the members that can be found by following the relation.

**Domain:** `ldes:Relation`

**Range:** `xsd:dateTime` with a timezone

### ldes:timeUntil ### {#timeUntil}

Exclusive upper bound of the `ldes:timestampPath` value of the members that can be found by following the relation.

**Domain:** `ldes:Relation`

**Range:** `xsd:dateTime` with a timezone

### ldes:sequenceFrom ### {#sequenceFrom}

Inclusive lower bound of the `ldes:sequencePath` value of the members that can be found by following the relation.

**Domain:** `ldes:Relation`

**Range:** an `xsd`-typed literal

### ldes:sequenceUntil ### {#sequenceUntil}

Exclusive upper bound of the `ldes:sequencePath` value of the members that can be found by following the relation.

**Domain:** `ldes:Relation`

**Range:** an `xsd`-typed literal

## Membership ## {#membership}

How the member identifier is found in each member message. At most one of the indirect membership properties can be set on an `ldes:EventStream`. When none is set, direct membership applies.

### ldes:member ### {#member}

Direct membership: a triple `<ES> ldes:member ?m` in the member message states which entity is the member. Aligned with `tree:member`.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

### ldes:memberGraph ### {#memberGraph}

Indirect membership: when `true`, the member identifier is the name of the only named graph in each member message.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** `xsd:boolean`

### ldes:memberType ### {#memberType}

Indirect membership: the member identifier is the only subject in each member message that has this `rdf:type`.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** `rdfs:Class`

### ldes:memberPath ### {#memberPath}

Indirect membership: the member identifier is the only subject in each member message from which this path leads to a value.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

**Range:** a [SHACL property path](https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/#property-paths)

## ldes:retentionPolicy ## {#retentionPolicy}

Links to a retention policy.

**Domain:** `ldes:EventStream`

Issue: In LDES 1.0 the domain was the root node or a view description. Moving the retention policy to the LDES is a change that needs to be discussed.

**Range:** `ldes:RetentionPolicy`

## ldes:RetentionPolicy ## {#RetentionPolicy}

The class for a retention policy that indicates how long members are preserved in this view.

### ldes:startingFrom ### {#startingFrom}

The view only keeps members starting from a certain timestamp.

**Domain:** `ldes:RetentionPolicy`

**Range:** `xsd:dateTime` with a timezone

### ldes:versionDuration ### {#versionDuration}

The view keeps versions (for which `ldes:versionAmount` MUST be set) only for a specific time window. 

**Domain:** `ldes:RetentionPolicy`

**Range:** `xsd:duration`

### ldes:versionAmount ### {#versionAmount}

The number of versions to keep. This MUST be greater than 0.

**Domain:** `ldes:RetentionPolicy`

**Range:** `xsd:integer`

### ldes:versionDeleteDuration ### {#versionDeleteDuration}

The view only keeps its deletions for a certain duration.

**Domain:** `ldes:RetentionPolicy`

**Range:** `xsd:duration`

### ldes:fullLogDuration ### {#fullLogDuration}

The view keeps its full log for a certain duration.

**Domain:** `ldes:RetentionPolicy`

**Range:** `xsd:duration`

## Terms for versioning and transactions on top of ldes:EventStream ## {#versioning-transactions}

### ldes:versionCreatePath ### {#versionCreatePath}

Path whose object indicates that the member represents a create. Defaults to `rdf:type`.

### ldes:versionUpdatePath ### {#versionUpdatePath}

Path whose object indicates that the member represents an update. Defaults to `rdf:type`.

### ldes:versionDeletePath ### {#versionDeletePath}

Path whose object indicates that the member represents a delete. Defaults to `rdf:type`.

### ldes:versionCreateObject ### {#versionCreateObject}

If the object at `ldes:versionCreatePath` equals this value, the member represents a create.

### ldes:versionUpdateObject ### {#versionUpdateObject}

If the object at `ldes:versionUpdatePath` equals this value, the member represents an update.

### ldes:versionDeleteObject ### {#versionDeleteObject}

If the object at `ldes:versionDeletePath` equals this value, the member represents a delete.

### ldes:transactionPath ### {#transactionPath}

Path whose object indicates whether the member is part of a transaction.

### ldes:transactionFinalizedPath ### {#transactionFinalizedPath}

Path indicating whether the transaction has been finalized.

### ldes:transactionFinalizedObject ### {#transactionFinalizedObject}

If the object at `ldes:transactionFinalizedPath` equals this value, the member indicates the transaction has been finalized.

# Alignment with TREE # {#tree-alignment}

LDES 2.0 no longer uses the TREE vocabulary within its pages. The following table lists the alignments, as published in the [Turtle version](vocabulary.ttl).

The alignment of the terms that are needed to traverse an LDES is made with `rdfs:subClassOf` and `rdfs:subPropertyOf` axioms, which are in the profile of OWL 2 RL. After an OWL 2 RL reasoner has processed an LDES page together with `vocabulary.ttl`, a [TREE](https://w3id.org/tree/specification) client sees:
 * every `ldes:Page` as a `tree:Node`;
 * every `ldes:relation` as a `tree:relation` to a `tree:Relation`, with the `ldes:page` as its `tree:node`.

Such a relation has no more specific TREE type, so a TREE client will follow it without being able to prune: the TREE specification states that a client follows a relation of a type it does not know. To also allow a TREE client to prune, a producer can add TREE relation types, `tree:path` and `tree:value` to the same relation, see [relations](index.html#relations) in the main specification.

The other terms are aligned using `skos:closeMatch`, as an inference cannot capture the difference in semantics:
 * `tree:view` cannot be inferred, as nothing in an LDES page points from the LDES to the root page: the IRI of the LDES dereferences to it. A TREE client will have to be given the root page.
 * `ldes:member` and `ldes:shape` are not declared to be subproperties of `tree:member` and `tree:shape`, as the domain of those properties is `tree:Collection`, which is a `dcat:Dataset`. A reasoner would then infer that the `ldes:EventStream`, which is a `dcat:Distribution`, is a dataset too. Members that are found using indirect membership cannot be inferred as `tree:member` in any case.

Issue: Do we want the subproperty axioms for `ldes:member` and `ldes:shape` as well, accepting that a reasoner will derive that the LDES is also a `tree:Collection`? Or a separate, optional alignment file?

<table class="simple">
  <thead><tr><th>LDES 2.0</th><th>TREE</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>ldes:EventStream</code></td><td><code>tree:Collection</code> (loosely; an <code>ldes:EventStream</code> is a <code>dcat:Distribution</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ldes:Page</code></td><td><code>tree:Node</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>(the LDES IRI dereferences to the root page)</td><td><code>tree:view</code> (removed)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ldes:shape</code></td><td><code>tree:shape</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ldes:member</code></td><td><code>tree:member</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ldes:Relation</code>, <code>ldes:relation</code>, <code>ldes:page</code></td><td><code>tree:Relation</code>, <code>tree:relation</code>, <code>tree:node</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ldes:timeFrom</code>, <code>ldes:timeUntil</code>, <code>ldes:sequenceFrom</code>, <code>ldes:sequenceUntil</code></td><td><code>tree:GreaterThanOrEqualToRelation</code> and <code>tree:LessThanRelation</code> with <code>tree:path</code> and <code>tree:value</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>(the LDES itself)</td><td><code>tree:viewDescription</code> and <code>ldes:EventSource</code> (removed)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
